{# ============================================================================
   PEBBLE SCROLLING CARDS — two product columns and a headline that move together
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ┌──────────┐                                    ┌──────────┐
     │          │            وصل حديثاً               │          │  ← the second
     │  product │      ‾‾‾‾ناعمة ومرحة،‾‾‾‾          │          │    column sits
     │          │        بلون الليلك                 │  product │    125px lower
     │ ┌──────┐ │      نصّ قصير في سطرين              │          │
     │ │ chip │ │        ( تسوّقي الآن ▸ )            │ ┌──────┐ │
     └─┴──────┴─┘                                    └─┴──────┴─┘

   ── One block is one BEAT, not one card ──
   The two photographs and the headline change together, so they belong to the
   same block: a line of copy, the phrase inside it that gets a highlight, the
   colour of that highlight, and the product each column shows. Splitting them
   into three lists would have made "which card goes with which line" a thing
   the merchant has to keep in their head.

   Measured off the reference at 1440px: a 1200 container split 347 / 505 / 348,
   a 3:4 card, a 40px headline on a 46px line, and pastel highlights
   (#D3C9FD, #B2DFE6) sitting behind the words rather than around them.

   ── The scroll IS the control ──
   The section is taller than the screen and its contents are `position: sticky`,
   so it pins while the page moves through it and the scroll distance becomes the
   timeline. The headline glides CONTINUOUSLY with that distance — it is scrubbed,
   not stepped — and the cards cross-fade at each halfway point.

   That is what the reference does, and it is not the same thing as a carousel on
   a timer: the shopper sets the pace, nothing changes while they are reading, and
   scrolling back takes them back. `advance_on: time` is there for a merchant who
   wants this mid-page without pinning it.

   ── The headline is a masked column, not a fade ──
   The lines are stacked and translated; the mask shows a little over two of
   them, so the tail of the previous beat and the head of the next are visible
   at the edges. That is what makes it read as one continuous sentence being
   written rather than as three separate captions.

   ── What the card's button does ──
   Adds to the cart when the product has no options, and goes to the product
   page when it does — the same rule the cart's cross-sell uses, for the same
   reason: a product with a size cannot be added blind, and a button that
   silently picks one for the shopper is worse than a button that asks.

   All styling lives in assets/style.css → "15.13.5 SCROLLING CARDS".
   ========================================================================= #}

{% set id = widget.id %}
{% set d = widget.data %}
{# ── The cap, and why it is SIX ──
   This section's height IS its beat count: `--hy-sc-run` is
   `100vh + (n - 1) × scroll_per_beat`, so every beat a merchant adds is
   another screenful of scrolling. Measured at the default 70vh/beat:

       4 beats →  3.1 screens        10 beats →  7.3 screens
       6 beats →  4.5 screens        15 beats → 10.8 screens

   and at the setting's maximum of 140vh/beat those become 5.2, 8.0, 13.6 and
   20.6. Past six the section stops being a section and becomes a scroll trap
   the shopper cannot get out of, so the extras are not rendered. #}
{% set SC_MAX = 6 %}
{% set beats = (widget.blocks | default([])).slice(0, SC_MAX) %}
{% set count = beats | length %}

{% set eyebrow = d.eyebrow | default('') %}
{% set body = d.body | default('') %}
{% set ctaText = d.cta_text | default('') %}
{% set ctaUrl = d.cta_url | default('/shop') %}

{% set mode = d.advance_on | default('scroll') %}
{% set perBeat = d.scroll_per_beat | default(70) %}
{% set speed = d.autoplay_speed | default(4, true) %}

{% set ratio = d.card_ratio | default('3x4') %}
{% set offset = d.column_offset | default(125) %}
{% set showPrice = d.show_price | default(true) %}

{% set ratioMap = { '3x4': '3 / 4', '4x5': '4 / 5', '1x1': '1 / 1' } %}


{# ---- one product card ----
   `products` hands back an ARRAY even when the merchant picked one, so every
   call site takes the first. A block with nothing picked renders a placeholder
   tile rather than an empty column. #}
{% macro card(list, eager) %}
  {% set p = list[0] if list and (list | length) > 0 else null %}
  {% if p %}
    {% set img = p.images[0].fileUrl if p.images and (p.images | length) > 0 else '' %}
    {% set url = '/products/' ~ (p.slug | default(p.handle) | default(p._id)) %}
    {% set inStock = p.allowBackorder or (not p.trackQuantity) or p.variantsCount or (p.options | default([], true) | length) > 0 or p.quantity > 0 %}
    {% set hasVariants = (p.variantsCount and p.variantsCount > 0) or (p.options and (p.options | length) > 0) %}

    <div class="hy-sc-card">
      <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-sc-media" aria-label="{{ p.title }}">
        {% if img %}
          <img src="{{ img }}" alt="{{ p.title }}"
               {% if eager %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}/>
        {% endif %}
      </a>

      {# The chip is a sibling of the media, not a child of the link: it holds
         its own link and its own button, and an <a> inside an <a> is invalid
         markup that browsers resolve by closing the outer one early. #}
      <div class="hy-sc-chip">
        <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-sc-thumb" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
          {% if img %}<img src="{{ img }}" alt="" loading="lazy"/>{% endif %}
        </a>
        <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-sc-info">
          <span class="hy-sc-name">{{ p.title }}</span>
          {% if showPrice %}
            <span class="hy-sc-price">{{ p.pricing.price | default(0) | money }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </a>

        {% if inStock and not hasVariants %}
          <button type="button" class="hy-sc-buy"
                  @click="CartManager.add('{{ p._id }}', 1)">
            {{ t('products.add') }}
          </button>
        {% else %}
          <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-sc-buy">
            {{ t('products.shop') if hasVariants else t('pages.product.out_of_stock') }}
          </a>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="hy-sc-card" data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="hy-sc-media hy-sc-media--ph"></span>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}


{# ---- the second line, with its phrase picked out ----
   `replace` on the exact phrase, because the merchant types the words they want
   lit rather than wrapping them in markup they would have to get right. An
   empty or non-matching `highlight` leaves the line untouched, which is the
   right failure: a typo costs a highlight, never the sentence. #}
{% macro line2(s) %}
  {% if s.highlight and s.line_2 and s.line_2.indexOf(s.highlight) > -1 %}
    {{ s.line_2 | replace(s.highlight, '<mark class="hy-sc-mark">' ~ s.highlight ~ '</mark>') | safe }}
  {% else %}
    {{ s.line_2 | default('') }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}


<section id="hy-sc-{{ id }}" class="hy-sc hy-sc--{{ mode }}">
  <style>
    /* The `-set` suffix is load-bearing: this is an ID selector, so anything it
       writes outranks every class rule in the stylesheet, responsive ones
       included. The stylesheet reads these as the DESKTOP values and decides
       what the narrower breakpoints use. */
    #hy-sc-{{ id }} {
      --hy-sc-ratio-set: {{ ratioMap[ratio] | default('3 / 4') }};
      --hy-sc-offset-set: {{ offset }}px;
      {% if mode == 'scroll' and count > 1 %}
      /* The scroll timeline: one screen to read the first beat, then this much
         again for each one after it. */
      --hy-sc-run: calc(100vh + {{ (count - 1) * perBeat }}vh);
      {% endif %}
    }
    {# Top-level rules, NOT nested inside the block above: a rule inside a plain
       declaration block is CSS Nesting, which this theme does not assume. #}
    {% for b in beats %}
    #hy-sc-{{ id }} [data-hy-beat="{{ loop.index0 }}"] .hy-sc-mark {
      --hy-sc-mark: {{ b.data.highlight_color | default('color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 16%, var(--color-bg-primary))', true) }};
    }
    {% endfor %}
  </style>

  <div class="hy-sc-pin">
   <div class="hy-container">
    <div class="hy-sc-grid">

      {# ---- first column ---- #}
      <div class="hy-sc-col hy-sc-col--start">
        {% for b in beats %}
          <div class="hy-sc-slot {{ 'is-active' if loop.first }}" data-hy-slot="{{ loop.index0 }}">
            {{ card(b.data.product_start, loop.first) }}
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if count == 0 %}
          <div class="hy-sc-slot is-active">{{ card(null, true) }}</div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {# ---- centre ---- #}
      <div class="hy-sc-copy">
        {% if eyebrow %}<p class="hy-sc-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}

        {% if count > 0 %}
          {# The mask. Its height is two lines plus the sliver of the neighbours
             that makes the movement legible; the track inside it is translated
             by whole beats. #}
          <div class="hy-sc-ticker" aria-live="polite">
            <div class="hy-sc-track" id="hy-scTrack-{{ id }}">
              {% for b in beats %}
                <div class="hy-sc-beat" data-hy-beat="{{ loop.index0 }}">
                  <span class="hy-sc-line">{{ b.data.line_1 | default('') }}</span>
                  <span class="hy-sc-line">{{ line2(b.data) }}</span>
                </div>
              {% endfor %}
              {# The first beat again, so the wrap from the last to the first is
                 a continuation rather than a jump backwards through every
                 line. The script resets to 0 while this clone is on screen. #}
              {% if count > 1 %}
                <div class="hy-sc-beat" data-hy-beat="0" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="hy-sc-line">{{ beats[0].data.line_1 | default('') }}</span>
                  <span class="hy-sc-line">{{ line2(beats[0].data) }}</span>
                </div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if body %}
          {# ⚠️  A <div>, NOT a <p>. A `text` field comes back as block HTML and
             a <p> cannot contain a <p> — the browser closes the outer one and
             the copy becomes a SIBLING, out of reach of every style on it. #}
          <div class="hy-sc-body">{{ body | safe }}</div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if ctaText %}
          <a href="{{ ctaUrl }}" class="hy-btn hy-btn--lg hy-btn--pill hy-btn--arrow hy-btn--solid hy-sc-cta">
            <span>{{ ctaText }}</span>
            <i class="hy-btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="rtl-flip" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                   stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"
                   stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
            </i>
          </a>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {# ---- second column ---- #}
      <div class="hy-sc-col hy-sc-col--end">
        {% for b in beats %}
          <div class="hy-sc-slot {{ 'is-active' if loop.first }}" data-hy-slot="{{ loop.index0 }}">
            {{ card(b.data.product_end, loop.first) }}
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if count == 0 %}
          <div class="hy-sc-slot is-active">{{ card(null, true) }}</div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  /* ---- empty slots borrow the store's products ----
     A beat with nothing picked renders a skeleton card; HayatAuto (main.js)
     fills each one, in page order, with the next product the store has. The
     markup below mirrors the `card()` macro above — keep them together.

     The button starts as a link to the product and only becomes "add" once the
     FULL record confirms there are no options: the list payload carries none,
     and a product with options added blind lands in the cart with no variant. */
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('hy-sc-{{ id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    var L = { add: {{ t('products.add') | dump | safe }}, shop: {{ t('products.shop') | dump | safe }}, out: {{ t('pages.product.out_of_stock') | dump | safe }} };
    var showPrice = {{ 'true' if showPrice else 'false' }};

    function build(p, eager) {
      var A = window.HayatAuto, esc = HayatCard.esc;
      var url = A.url(p), img = A.img(p), title = esc(p.title);
      var pic = img ? '<img src="' + esc(img) + '" alt="' + title + '"' + (eager ? ' fetchpriority="high"' : ' loading="lazy"') + '/>' : '';
      return '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-sc-media" aria-label="' + title + '">' + pic + '</a>' +
        '<div class="hy-sc-chip">' +
          '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-sc-thumb" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">' + (img ? '<img src="' + esc(img) + '" alt="" loading="lazy"/>' : '') + '</a>' +
          '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-sc-info"><span class="hy-sc-name">' + title + '</span>' +
            (showPrice ? '<span class="hy-sc-price">' + esc(window.formatMoney((p.pricing && p.pricing.price) || 0)) + '</span>' : '') +
          '</a>' +
          '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-sc-buy">' + esc(L.shop) + '</a>' +
        '</div>';
    }

    function fill() {
      var slots = root.querySelectorAll('.hy-sc-card[data-hy-placeholder]');
      if (!slots.length || !window.HayatAuto) return;
      HayatAuto.take(slots.length).then(function (list) {
        list.forEach(function (p, i) {
          var card = slots[i];
          card.removeAttribute('data-hy-placeholder');
          card.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
          card.innerHTML = build(p, i === 0);
          HayatAuto.full(p).then(function (full) {
            var buy = card.querySelector('.hy-sc-buy');
            if (!buy) return;
            if (!HayatAuto.inStock(full)) { buy.textContent = L.out; return; }
            if (HayatAuto.hasOptions(full)) return;
            var btn = document.createElement('button');
            btn.type = 'button';
            btn.className = 'hy-sc-buy';
            btn.textContent = L.add;
            btn.addEventListener('click', function () { CartManager.add(full._id || p._id, 1); });
            buy.replaceWith(btn);
          });
        });
      });
    }
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', fill);
    } else {
      fill();
    }
  })();
</script>

<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('hy-sc-{{ id }}');
    if (!root || {{ count }} < 2) return;

    var track = document.getElementById('hy-scTrack-{{ id }}');
    var cols = root.querySelectorAll('.hy-sc-col');
    var total = {{ count | int }};
    var shown = -1;

    /* The ticker moves by whole BEATS, and a beat is two lines — so the step is
       measured off a rendered beat rather than computed from a line-height the
       font may not honour exactly. */
    function step() {
      var b = track && track.querySelector('.hy-sc-beat');
      return b ? b.offsetHeight : 0;
    }

    /* `t` is a POSITION, not an index: 1.5 means halfway between the second beat
       and the third. The ticker takes it whole so it glides; the cards round it,
       so they swap at the halfway point rather than drifting with it. */
    function render(t) {
      if (track) track.style.transform = 'translate3d(0,' + (-t * step()).toFixed(1) + 'px,0)';
      var i = Math.round(t);
      if (i < 0) i = 0;
      if (i > total - 1) i = total - 1;
      if (i === shown) return;
      shown = i;
      for (var c = 0; c < cols.length; c++) {
        var slots = cols[c].querySelectorAll('[data-hy-slot]');
        for (var s = 0; s < slots.length; s++) slots[s].classList.toggle('is-active', s === i);
      }
    }

    {% if mode == 'scroll' %}
    /* ---- scroll-scrubbed ----
       The section is taller than the screen and its contents are sticky, so the
       distance the page travels through it IS the timeline. Progress is measured
       against the part of the section the pin does NOT occupy, which is exactly
       the distance available to scrub.

       rAF-gated: `scroll` fires far more often than the screen repaints, and the
       transform it writes only lands once per frame anyway. */
    var pin = root.querySelector('.hy-sc-pin');
    var ticking = false;

    /* The pin is only as tall as its contents, so it sticks at whatever offset
       centres it on screen. Written on resize only — a scroll never changes it. */
    var stickTop = 0;
    function place() {
      if (!pin) return;
      stickTop = Math.max(0, Math.round((window.innerHeight - pin.offsetHeight) / 2));
      root.style.setProperty('--hy-sc-top', stickTop + 'px');
    }

    function apply() {
      ticking = false;
      var runway = root.offsetHeight - (pin ? pin.offsetHeight : 0);
      if (runway <= 0) { render(0); return; }
      /* 0 when the pin sticks — the section's top reaching `stickTop` — and 1
         when it lets go, `runway` later. */
      var p = (stickTop - root.getBoundingClientRect().top) / runway;
      if (p < 0) p = 0;
      if (p > 1) p = 1;
      render(p * (total - 1));
    }

    function onScroll() {
      if (ticking) return;
      ticking = true;
      window.requestAnimationFrame(apply);
    }

    function relayout() { place(); apply(); }

    relayout();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', relayout);
    /* A reload restores the scroll position AFTER this runs, and bfcache
       restores it with no scroll event at all. `load` also re-places: the
       pin's height changes once its images arrive. */
    window.addEventListener('load', relayout);
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', apply);
    {% else %}
    /* ---- on a timer ----
       For a merchant who wants this mid-page without pinning it. The step is
       whole beats, so `render` is called on integers and the ticker snaps
       between them with its own transition rather than being scrubbed. */
    render(0);
    var at = 0;
    var reduce = document.documentElement.classList.contains('hy-no-motion') || (window.matchMedia
      && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);

    if (!reduce) {
      var timer = null;
      var start = function () {
        if (timer) return;
        timer = window.setInterval(function () {
          at = (at + 1) % total;
          render(at);
        }, {{ (speed * 1000) | int }});
      };
      var stop = function () { if (timer) { window.clearInterval(timer); timer = null; } };

      /* Only runs while it is on screen. A section rotating in a tab nobody is
         looking at is work the phone pays for and the shopper never sees. */
      if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        new IntersectionObserver(function (e) { e[0].isIntersecting ? start() : stop(); },
                                 { threshold: 0.2 }).observe(root);
      } else { start(); }

      root.addEventListener('mouseenter', stop);
      root.addEventListener('mouseleave', start);
      document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
        document.hidden ? stop() : start();
      });
    }
    {% endif %}

    /* The step is measured, so it has to be re-measured when the measurement can
       change — a web font swapping in moves every line. */
    if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) {
      document.fonts.ready.then(function () { shown = -1; {% if mode == 'scroll' %}apply(){% else %}render(at){% endif %}; });
    }
  })();
</script>

{# Per-section palette. Emits nothing unless `colors_enabled` is on, so the
   switch IS the revert. Must stay after the widget's own <style>. #}
{% ui "section-colors.njk", scope='#hy-sc-' ~ id, c=d %}
